From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:29:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): fold the phone drawer's primary nav into one strip

On a phone, the drawer's primary nav is a stack of 44px rows above the
session list. At phone width the always-on destinations (New session,
Automations, Inbox) now share one strip of equal-width icon-over-label
cells (at least 44px tall) in a rounded glass container: three rows of
about 134px become a strip of about 68px. The strip never scrolls:
flag-gated pages (Canvas, Usage) and extension pages, when enabled, stay
full-width rows directly below it.
Cell labels follow the Appearance interface font size.

Every item now renders through PrimaryNavLink, which takes a row or cell
layout, so both layouts share one definition per destination; a small
PrimaryNavStrip wraps the always-on three only on the phone drawer. The cells
keep their test ids, component ids, links, drawer closing and active
highlight; New keeps the accessible name "New session" and its
aria-keyshortcuts, and the Inbox count sits on the cell's corner with the
same label. The strip follows the overlay drawer layout (below 768px);
wider windows and the side-by-side layout on wide phones keep the
stacked rows.

Refs #13482

[Desidero: Automations stays unconditional (this base has no
automations_enabled gate), New session keeps the project prompt's click
handler from new-chat-project-prompt, and the drawer test leaves out
upstream's newer keyboard-dismissal tests and the test for automations
turned off]

Not upstream yet: proposed from feat/mobile-sidebar-nav-strip; drop this copy once it merges.

Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 55d7757d897c9123a54a86db8ca7318ea4e2dd5b)
